<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO no comment on U.S. buy report.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO no comment on U.S. buy report.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV said on Wednesday it had no comment on a newspaper report that it wanted to buy New York fund manager Weis, Peck and Greer.</p>
<p>&quot;At this time there's no comment,&quot; said ABN spokesman Tanno Massar.</p>
<p>Dutch daily Algemeen Dagblad said the Dutch bank was keen to buy the fund manager, which has $13 billion under management.</p>
<p>The ambitious bank has made no secret of the fact that it wants to expand in funds management and is looking to the United States for such an acquisition.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
